    "created_at": "2020-05-14T12:41:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-14T12:41:50Z",
    "body": "I found that IE and Edge actually lowercase the drive letter, and then incorrectly stick it to the host, e.g. `file://somehost/C:/test` becomes `file://somehostc:/test`. \r\n\r\nAlso it seems that Chrome on Mac does not support drive letters at all but treats them as ordinary path components. \r\n",
