    "body": "https://jsdom.github.io/whatwg-url/#url=ZmlsZTovLy8uL0N8&base=YWJvdXQ6Ymxhbms= on Chrome on Windows shows it matching the standard, with an output of `file:///C:` (protocol `file:`, pathname `/C:`).\r\n\r\nFeeding that output back in is idempotent, so at least that case is not problematic. I'm not sure whether any non-idempotent cases remain, now that https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1083031 is closed.",
